// examples/layout.ent, a library that lays boxes out inside boxes with
// reactive `for`s along a tree whose children are in an order (which box
// a box is in, and where among those in it), each running only where
// something it reads has changed; boxes may stand in the middle across
// their row or column, and float over another box, a layer above, also
// over one inside a box that floats. Inputs/layout_print.ent prints where
// a small window's boxes end up, and examples/layout_demo.ent, which
// draws one, compiles.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples %S/Inputs/layout_print.ent 2>/dev/null \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/../../examples/layout_demo.ent \
// RUN:     -I %S/../../devices -I %S/../../examples -o %t.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir --ent-lower-to-loops --convert-scf-to-cf \
// RUN:     --convert-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
// RUN:   | mlir-translate --mlir-to-llvmir > %t.ll
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LLVM --input-file=%t.ll
// A pass that follows its events has its body in several places, and
// for every kind of box: one function that they call, not a copy in
// each, and a box that is looked up is found by a table, not by a branch
// for every kind. (Three times this much, without.)
// RUN: wc -l < %t.ll | awk '{ exit !($1 < 450000) }'

// LLVM-DAG: define {{.*}}void @ent_connect_layout.Inside(
// LLVM-DAG: declare float @ent_window_text_min_width(
// LLVM-DAG: define {{.*}}void @ent_part_0(
// LLVM-DAG: declare void @ent_window_rect(float, float, float, float, i32)

// The side bar is 200 wide and as high as the window's inside; the rest
// has the width that is left, 800 - 2 * 10 - 200 - 10. The header is as
// high as its higher button and its padding, the body has what is left
// under it, and its columns share its width less their gap.
// CHECK:      1: root 0.0 0.0 800.0 600.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: rest 220.0 10.0 570.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: header 220.0 10.0 570.0 40.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: body 220.0 56.0 570.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: left 220.0 56.0 275.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: right 515.0 56.0 275.0 534.0 layer 0
// In the middle across the side bar: (200 - 2 * 8 - 40) / 2 in from its
// padding.
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: item 90.0 18.0 40.0 20.0 layer 0
// The badge floats 4 in and 2 down from the header's corner, a layer
// above it, as big as the dot in it and its padding.
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: dot 227.0 15.0 10.0 8.0 layer 1
// (A pin inside the mark, and a speck that floats over the pin: a box
// that floats three deep is placed in the same frame too.)
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: pin 228.0 16.0 2.0 2.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: side 10.0 10.0 200.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: ok 225.0 15.0 60.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: cancel 288.0 15.0 90.0 30.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: badge 224.0 12.0 16.0 14.0 layer 1
// And the mark over the dot, which is inside the badge that floats: 1
// in and down from it, another layer above.
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: mark 228.0 16.0 4.0 4.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: speck 229.0 17.0 1.0 1.0 layer 3
// A narrower side bar: everything next to it moves and widens, and the
// badge goes with the header, the dot with the badge and the mark with
// the dot, in the same frame.
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: root 0.0 0.0 800.0 600.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: rest 120.0 10.0 670.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: header 120.0 10.0 670.0 40.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: body 120.0 56.0 670.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: left 120.0 56.0 325.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: right 465.0 56.0 325.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: item 40.0 18.0 40.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: dot 127.0 15.0 10.0 8.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: pin 128.0 16.0 2.0 2.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: side 10.0 10.0 100.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: ok 125.0 15.0 60.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: cancel 188.0 15.0 90.0 30.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: badge 124.0 12.0 16.0 14.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: mark 128.0 16.0 4.0 4.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 2: speck 129.0 17.0 1.0 1.0 layer 3
// The body's two below one another: each as wide as it, sharing its
// height.
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: root 0.0 0.0 800.0 600.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: rest 120.0 10.0 670.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: header 120.0 10.0 670.0 40.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: body 120.0 56.0 670.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: left 120.0 56.0 670.0 257.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: right 120.0 333.0 670.0 257.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: item 40.0 18.0 40.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: dot 127.0 15.0 10.0 8.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: pin 128.0 16.0 2.0 2.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: side 10.0 10.0 100.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: ok 125.0 15.0 60.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: cancel 188.0 15.0 90.0 30.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: badge 124.0 12.0 16.0 14.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: mark 128.0 16.0 4.0 4.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3: speck 129.0 17.0 1.0 1.0 layer 3
// The first button given a later slot than the second: they change
// places.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: root 0.0 0.0 800.0 600.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: rest 120.0 10.0 670.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: header 120.0 10.0 670.0 40.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: body 120.0 56.0 670.0 534.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: left 120.0 56.0 670.0 257.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: right 120.0 333.0 670.0 257.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: item 40.0 18.0 40.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: dot 127.0 15.0 10.0 8.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: pin 128.0 16.0 2.0 2.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: side 10.0 10.0 100.0 580.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: ok 218.0 15.0 60.0 20.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: cancel 125.0 15.0 90.0 30.0 layer 0
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: badge 124.0 12.0 16.0 14.0 layer 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: mark 128.0 16.0 4.0 4.0 layer 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 4: speck 129.0 17.0 1.0 1.0 layer 3
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
